      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "The edge length of a square can be expressed in two different ways, so we can set them equal to each other and solve for $x$:\n\n$4x-15 = 20-3x$\n\nAdding $3x$ to both sides gives us:\n\n$7x-15 = 20$\n\nAdding $15$ to both sides gives us:\n\n$7x = 35$\n\nDividing both sides by $7$ gives us:\n\n$x = 5$\n\nNow that we know $x$, we can substitute it back into either expression for the edge length to find the length of the square:\n\n$4x-15 = 4(5)-15 = 20-15 = 5$\n\nThe area of the square is the square of the edge length:\n\n$5^2 = \\boxed{25}$",
