    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of the square, we need to first determine the length of its side. According to the problem, the length of the side of the square can be expressed in two different ways: $4x-15$ meters and $20-3x$ meters. Since both expressions represent the same length, we can set them equal to each other and solve for $x$.\n\n$$4x-15 = 20-3x$$\n\nAdding $3x$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$4x+3x-15 = 20$$\n\nCombining like terms:\n\n$$7x-15 = 20$$\n\nAdding $15$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$7x = 35$$\n\nDividing both sides by $7$:\n\n$$x = 5$$\n\nNow that we have the value of $x$, we can substitute it back into either expression for the length of the side of the square to find the actual length. Let's use $4x-15$:\n\n$$4(5)-15 = 20-3(5)$$\n\n$$20-15 = 20-15$$\n\n$$5 = 5$$\n\nThe length of the side of the square is $5$ meters. To find the area of the square, we need to square the length of the side:\n\nArea = $(5)^2 = 25$ square meters.\n\nSo, the area of the square is $\\boxed{25}$ square meters.",
