    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the area of the square, we need to determine the length of its side. Given that the edge of the square can be expressed as \\(4x-15\\) meters or as \\(20-3x\\) meters, we can set these two expressions equal to each other and solve for \\(x\\).\n\nFirst, we set the expressions equal to each other:\n\\[\n4x - 15 = 20 - 3x\n\\]\n\nNext, we solve for \\(x\\). To do this, we first add \\(3x\\) to both sides of the equation:\n\\[\n4x + 3x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\\[\n7x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\nThen, we add 15 to both sides:\n\\[\n7x = 35\n\\]\n\nFinally, we divide both sides by 7:\n\\[\nx = 5\n\\]\n\nNow that we have the value of \\(x\\), we can substitute it back into either of the original expressions to find the length of the side of the square. We use \\(4x - 15\\):\n\\[\n4(5) - 15 = 20 - 15 = 5\n\\]\n\nSo, the length of the side of the square is 5 meters. The area of the square is the side length squared:\n\\[\n5^2 = 25\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is \\(\\boxed{25}\\) square meters.",
