      "text": "To find the area of the square, we first need to determine the length of one of its sides. Given that the length of one side is expressed as both \\(4x - 15\\) meters and \\(20 - 3x\\) meters, we can set these two expressions equal to each other and solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[4x - 15 = 20 - 3x\\]\n\nFirst, we combine like terms by adding \\(3x\\) to both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[4x + 3x - 15 = 20\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[7x - 15 = 20\\]\n\nNext, we add 15 to both sides to isolate the term with \\(x\\):\n\n\\[7x = 35\\]\n\nThen, we divide both sides by 7 to solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[x = 5\\]\n\nNow that we have the value of \\(x\\), we can substitute it back into one of the expressions for the side length of the square. Using \\(4x - 15\\):\n\n\\[4(5) - 15 = 20 - 15 = 5\\]\n\nSo, the length of one side of the square is 5 meters. The area of a square is given by the square of the length of one of its sides. Therefore, the area is:\n\n\\[5^2 = 25\\]\n\nThus, the area of the square is \\(\\boxed{25}\\) square meters.",
